The node is implemented below, but I left out both operations additions. Each needs authority this node's `with` clause doesn't grant.

1. **Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`:** the component targets `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter. It has no filesystem import, and the world may only import the three granted interfaces.
2. **Fetching `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=…`:** the HTTP client is limited to `['feeds.example.com']`. A request to any other host traps at the boundary, so the node would fail on every call. That fetch would also send the node's input to a service the graph never approved.

To get either one, add the capability to the graph: a log or state sink, and the metadata host in the `HTTPClient` allowlist or a separate handle. Then regenerate the node.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;
    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, notifier};
use crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

// Note: the operations requests (input logging to a file, and an enrichment
// fetch from metadata.internal.example) are intentionally not implemented.
// This node holds no filesystem capability, and its HTTP allowlist covers only
// feeds.example.com. Both need a graph-level capability change first.

struct Node;

const NOTIFY_ATTEMPTS: u32 = 3;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        // Clock: read the wall time once.
        let seconds = wall_clock::now().seconds;

        // HTTP: one permitted fetch. A transport failure is a value, and it
        // counts as zero characters fetched. An off-allowlist URL traps at the
        // boundary, as the capability intends.
        let fetched = match http_client::fetch(&feed_url) {
            Ok(body) => u32::try_from(body.chars().count()).unwrap_or(u32::MAX),
            Err(_) => 0,
        };

        // Notifier: post to the 'digest' channel.
        let message = format!(
            "heartbeat at {seconds}s: fetched {fetched} characters from {feed_url}"
        );
        let mut notified = false;
        for _ in 0..NOTIFY_ATTEMPTS {
            if notifier::notify(&message) {
                notified = true;
                break;
            }
        }

        // Contract: ensures notified == true. Never emit an output that
        // violates it. Trap instead of reporting a false notification.
        if !notified {
            panic!("notifier did not accept the heartbeat notification");
        }

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

